<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67022" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετάφρενον</span></b> , τό, prop.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>part behind the
			midriff</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ τὰς φρένας</span>),
				<i>broad of the back</i>: hence, generally, <i>back</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταφρένῳ ἐν δόρυ πῆξεν ὤμων
					μεσσηγύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.40
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				56
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἠδὲ καὶ ὤμω πλῆξεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.265
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἠδὲ καὶ ὤμους</span> (of a
			woman) <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.528
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Acut.</u>
				66
			</span></i>; in pl., of a single person, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.428
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤμους καὶ μετάφρενα</span>, of
			a woman, <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				29
			</span></i>. cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				10.32
			</span></i>. — 
				Ep.
			 word, used by <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				352a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Phgn.</u>
				810b25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMeretr.</u>
				4.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μεταξὺ τοῦ νώτου καὶ
					ὀσφύος κατὰ τὴν τῶν φρενῶν πρόσφυσιν</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				90
			</span></i>.</div>
